{
  "id": "COMPOUND:10898 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Tucaresol is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Tucaresol acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, N-Methyltyramine, and Botryorhodine C, all of which are themselves targets of the choline transporter. This indicates that the choline transporter may be a downstream effector of these metabolic pathways, potentially modulating choline uptake in response to the presence of these compounds. The consistent involvement of the choline transporter across different targets implies a potential role in the cellular response to these molecules, possibly through a shared regulatory mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights the choline transporter's involvement in a network of metabolic and signaling processes, underscoring its importance in the broader context of cellular function and drug action.",
